warning[iterator-traits]: `iterate` on `Countdown` without `eltype`; `collect` builds `Vector{Any}`
  --> src/IteratorTraitsPositive.jl:10:1
   |
10 | Base.iterate(countdown::Countdown, count::Int = countdown.start) = count < 1 ? nothing : (count, count - 1)
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^ element type defaults to `Any`
   |
   = why: `IteratorEltype` is `HasEltype`, so `collect` trusts `eltype`; Base default `eltype` is `Any`
   = fix: define `Base.eltype(::Type{<:Countdown})`, or `Base.IteratorEltype(::Type{<:Countdown}) = Base.EltypeUnknown()`   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain iterator-traits
   = note: warn from performance group, library preset
   = note: opt out with `# corset: allow iterator-traits -- <reason>`

